      <reaction id="mw49922564_34d3_45b5_b0c7_06d0438277d1" name="Reaction_349" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">CA19-9 secretion by live cancer cells (clone-weighted C1 + f_ca199_C2*C2). Damage suppression applies to the SENSITIVE clone ONLY: sec = k_ca199_sec * (C1/(1 + k_sec_suppress*C_dmg/cell) + f_ca199_C2*C2). The resistant clone escapes it, on the same warrant that gives it an r_resist-fold higher IC50 - a clone tolerant enough to survive chemotherapy is not the clone being driven into therapy-induced senescence, and CA19-9 is a differentiation antigen, so the shedding change tracks the damage rather than the drug. Before 2026-07-29 the 1/(1+k*D) factor multiplied BOTH clone terms, which made the marker un-reboundable: therapy runs continuously, so damage never clears, so the C2 sweep could not show up in CA19-9. Ablation measured that directly - removing suppression GAINED rebounds (38.8% -> 45.8%, +19 draws net) while removing resistance LOST them (38.8% -> 6.2%, -85), i.e. suppression was masking the mechanism that produces rebound rather than competing with it. See results/2026-07-29_resistance/.</body>
        </notes>
        <listOfProducts>
          <speciesReference species="mw10ef9c7e_26fc_4421_a8e7_761e24665387" stoichiometry="1"/>
        </listOfProducts>
        <kineticLaw>
          <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
            <apply>
              <times/>
              <ci> mw6dfdb045_88fc_4f29_a3bc_28f9914fb0f5 </ci>
              <apply>
                <plus/>
                <apply>
                  <divide/>
                  <ci> mwd7b3f48c_b5ce_4201_bf18_87b588f9c924 </ci>
                  <apply>
                    <plus/>
                    <cn type="integer"> 1 </cn>
                    <apply>
                      <times/>
                      <ci> mw7f50e6ed_5bfc_46ec_a5e2_0c40683d8626 </ci>
                      <apply><divide/><ci> mwda3c0000_0002_4000_a000_da39c0000002 </ci><ci> mw0ebcbcfd_1ae1_4b65_978f_4079890aa5d9 </ci></apply>
                    </apply>
                  </apply>
                </apply>
                <apply>
                  <times/>
                  <ci> mw80795b53_ecc5_425e_b95c_7a506f6049dd </ci>
                  <ci> mwe243ce15_95b9_40f2_8f29_3135d95a73fe </ci>
                </apply>
              </apply>
            </apply>
          </math>
        </kineticLaw>
      </reaction>
